{"lecture": "L11", "note": "public on purpose (Can 11.11): question 1 with solutions and pictures", "open": [{"student": {"parts": [{"n": 1, "utility": "<math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>", "budget": "<div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></div>"}, {"n": 2, "utility": "<math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>", "budget": "<div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></div>"}, {"n": 3, "utility": "<math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>", "budget": "<div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></div>"}, {"n": 4, "utility": "<math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>", "budget": "<div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></math></div><div><math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></div>"}, {"n": 5, "utility": "<math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "budget": "<div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></math></div><div><math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></div>"}]}, "teacher": {"parts": [{"n": 1, "caption": "", "solution": "<h4>The budget</h4><p><div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></div></p><h4>What the utility says</h4><p><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, <math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p>Bang for the buck: compare <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mfrac></math> with <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mfrac></math>, using each piece's own prices. Higher on <math><mi>x</mi></math>: more <math><mi>x</mi></math>. Equal: stop.</p><h4>Piece 1: <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></h4><p>Equal bang: <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> = <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, so <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Put this into the line: <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, so <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p>That is on this piece.</p><p>Bang for the buck at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mn>8</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mn>0</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so more <math><mi>x</mi></math>; at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mn>0</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mn>8</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so less <math><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><h4>Where it stops</h4><p>Bang for the buck stops at one point only, <math><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. So no comparison of utilities is needed.</p><h4>Answer</h4><p><b>The best bundle is <math><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, with <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>.</b></p>", "picture": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"budget pieces and bang for the buck\" style=\"font-size:12px\"><defs><clipPath id=\"b440452938\"><rect x=\"34\" y=\"10\" width=\"414\" height=\"294\"/></clipPath></defs><polygon points=\"34.0,304.0 34.0,36.7 410.4,304.0\" fill=\"#D9480F\" fill-opacity=\".10\"/><g clip-path=\"url(#b440452938)\" fill=\"none\"><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"36.7\" x2=\"410.4\" y2=\"304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><polyline points=\"36.6,-9414.8 39.2,-4555.5 4