><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"304.0\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"10.0\" stroke=\"#111\"/><polyline points=\"34.0,36.7 410.4,304.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"2.6\"/><line x1=\"410.4\" y1=\"304.0\" x2=\"410.4\" y2=\"308.0\" stroke=\"#111\"/><text x=\"410.4\" y=\"319.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text><line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"36.7\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"36.7\" stroke=\"#111\"/><text x=\"28.0\" y=\"40.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">8</text><circle cx=\"34.0\" cy=\"36.7\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"410.4\" cy=\"304.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\"/><polygon points=\"133.8,107.6 122.2,104.5 127.1,97.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><polygon points=\"310.6,233.1 322.2,236.2 317.3,243.1\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"222.2\" cy=\"170.4\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#111\"/><text x=\"227.2\" y=\"165.4\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">(4, 4)</text><text x=\"38.1\" y=\"118.5\" font-size=\"10\">at (0, 8): 8 vs 0</text><text x=\"226.3\" y=\"252.2\" font-size=\"10\">at (8, 0): 0 vs 8</text></svg>", "picture_note": "Arrows: which way bang for the buck pushes. A label such as \"at (0, 12): 6 vs 0\" means that at that point the bang is 6 on x against 0 on y. With several pieces it starts with the piece number."}, {"n": 2, "caption": "Both prices double. The new budget below is divided through by 2.", "solution": "<h4>The change</h4><p>Both prices double. The new budget below is divided through by 2.</p><h4>Before</h4><p>The best was <math><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, with <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math> at <math><mn>16</mn></math>.</p><h4>The new budget</h4><p><div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></div></p><h4>What the utility says</h4><p><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, <math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p>Bang for the buck: compare <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mfrac></math> with <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mfrac></math>, using each piece's own prices. Higher on <math><mi>x</mi></math>: more <math><mi>x</mi></math>. Equal: stop.</p><h4>Piece 1: <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></h4><p>Equal bang: <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> = <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, so <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Put this into the line: <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, so <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>That is on this piece.</p><p>Bang for the buck at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so more <math><mi>x</mi></math>; at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so less <math><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><h4>Where it stops</h4><p>Bang for the buck stops at one point only, <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. So no comparison of utilities is needed.</p><h4>Answer</h4><p><b>The best bundle is <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, with <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</b></p><h4>What changed</h4><p><b>The answer changes.</b> Utility falls from <math><mn>16</mn></math> to <math><mn>4</mn></math>.</p>", "picture": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"budget pieces and bang for the buck\" style=\"font-size:12px\"><defs><clipPath id=\"b3477296202\"><rect x=\"34\" y=\"10\" width=\"414\" height=\"294\"/></clipPath></defs><polygon points=\"34.0,304.0 34.0,170.4 222.2,304.0\" fill=\"#D9480F\" fill-opacity=\".10\"/><g clip-path=\"url(#b3477296202)\" fill=\"none\"><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"170.4\" x2=\"222.2\" y2=\"304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><polyline points=\"34.0,36.7 410.4,304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" stroke-opacity=\".6\"/><polyline points=\"36.6,-2125.7 39.2,-910.9 41.8,-505.9 44.4,-303.4 46.9,-181.9 49.5,-101.0 52.1,-43.1 54.7,0.3 57.3,34.0 59.9,61.0 62.5,83.1 65.1,101.5 67.6,117.1 70.2,130.4 72.8,142.0 75.4,152.1 78.0,161.1 80.6,169.0 83.2,176.1 85.8,182.5 88.3,188.3 90.9,193.6 93.5,198.4 96.1,202.8 98.7,206.8 101.3,210.5 103.9,214.0 106.5,217.2 109.0,220.2 111.6,223.0 114.2,225.6 116.8,228.1 119.4,230.4 122.0,232.5 124.6,234.6 127.2,236.5 129.7,238.3 132.3,240.1 134.9,241.7 137.5,243.3 140.1,244.7 142.7,246.1 145.3,247.5 147.9,248.8 150.4,250.0 153.0,251.2 155.6,252.3 158.2,253.4 160.8,254.4 163.4,255.4 166.0,256.4 168.6,257.3 171.1,258.2 173.7,259.0 176.3,259.8 178.9,260.6 181.5,261.4 184.1,262.1 186.7,262.8 189.3,263.5 191.8,264.2 194.4,264.8 197.0,265.4 199.6,266.0 202.2,266.6 204.8,267.2 207.4,267.7 210.0,268.3 212.5,268.8 215.1,269.3 217.7,269.8 220.3,270.3 222.9,270.7 225.5,271.2 228.1,271.6 230.7,272.0 233.2,272.4 235.8,272.8 238.4,273.2 241.0,273.6 243.6,274.0 246.2,274.4 248.8,274.7 251.4,275.1 253.9,275.4 256.5,275.7 259.1,276.1 261.7,276.4 264.3,276.7 266.9,277.0 269.5,277.3 272.1,277.6 274.6,277.9 277.2,278.2 279.8,278.4 282.4,278.7 285.0,279.0 287.6,279.2 290.2,279.5 292.8,279.7 295.3,279.9 297.9,280.2 300.5,280.4 303.1,280.6 305.7,280.9 308.3,281.1 310.9,281.3 313.5,281.5 316.0,281.7 318.6,281.9 321.2,282.1 323.8,282.3 326.4,282.5 329.0,282.7 331.6,282.9 334.2,283.1 336.7,283.2 339.3,283.4 341.9,283.6 344.5,283.8 347.1,283.9 349.7,284.1 352.3,284.2 354.9,284.4 357.4,284.6 360.0,284.7 362.6,284.9 365.2,285.0 367.8,285.2 370.4,285.3 373.0,285.5 375.6,285.6 378.1,285.7 380.7,285.9 383.3,286.0 385.9,286.1 388.5,286.3 391.1,286.4 393.7,286.5 396.3,286.6 398.8,286.8 401.4,286.9 404.0,287.0 406.6,287.1 409.2,287.2 411.8,287.4 414.4,287.5 417.0,287.6 419.5,287.7 422.1,287.8 424.7,287.9 427.3,288.0 429.9,288.1 432.5,288.2 435.1,288.3 437.7,288.4 440.2,288.5 442.8,288.6 445.4,288.7 448.0,288.8\" stroke=\"#0062C4\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/></g><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"304.0\" x2=\"448.0\" y2=\"304.0\" stroke=\"#111\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"304.0\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"10.0\" stroke=\"#111\"/><polyline points=\"34.0,170.4 222.2,304.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"2.6\"/><line x1=\"222.2\" y1=\"304.0\" x2=\"222.2\" y2=\"308.0\" stroke=\"#111\"/><text x=\"222.2\" y=\"319.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"170.4\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"170.4\" stroke=\"#111\"/><text x=\"28.0\" y=\"173.9\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><circle cx=\"34.0\" cy=\"170.4\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"222.2\" cy=\"304.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\"/><polygon points=\"86.7,207.9 75.1,204.8 80.0,197.9\" fill=\"#111\"/><polygon points=\"169.4,266.5 181.0,269.6 176.1,276.5\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"128.1\" cy=\"237.2\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#111\"/><text x=\"133.1\" y=\"232.2\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">(2, 2)</text><line x1=\"81.0\" y1=\"203.8\" x2=\"95.0\" y2=\"189.8\" stroke=\"#777\" stroke-width=\".6\"/><text x=\"95.0\" y=\"189.8\" font-size=\"10\">at (0, 4): 2 vs 0</text><text x=\"85.1\" y=\"285.6\" font-size=\"10\">at (4, 0): 0 vs 2</text></svg>", "picture_note": "Arrows: which way bang for the buck pushes. A label such as \"at (0, 12): 6 vs 0\" means that at that point the bang is 6 on x against 0 on y. With several pieces it starts with the piece number."}, {"n": 3, "caption": "The price of x goes from 2 to 1.", "solution": "<h4>The change</h4><p>The price of x goes from 2 to 1.</p><h4>Before</h4><p>The best was <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, with <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math> at <math><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><h4>The new budget</h4><p><div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></div></p><h4>What the utility says</h4><p><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, <math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p>Bang for the buck: compare <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mfrac></math> with <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mfrac></math>, using each piece's own prices. Higher on <math><mi>x</mi></math>: more <math><mi>x</mi></math>. Equal: stop.</p><h4>Piece 1: <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></h4><p>Equal bang: <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> = <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, so <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math>. Put this into the line: <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, so <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>That is on this piece.</p><p>Bang for the buck at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mn>4</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so more <math><mi>x</mi></math>; at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mn>0</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so less <math><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><h4>Where it stops</h4><p>Bang for the buck stops at one point only, <math><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. So no comparison of utilities is needed.</p><h4>Answer</h4><p><b>The best bundle is <math><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, with <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>.</b></p><h4>What changed</h4><p><b>The answer changes.</b> Utility rises from <math><mn>4</mn></math> to <math><mn>8</mn></math>.</p>", "picture": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"budget pieces and bang for the buck\" style=\"font-size:12px\"><defs><clipPath id=\"b576727274\"><rect x=\"34\" y=\"10\" width=\"414\" height=\"294\"/></clipPath></defs><polygon points=\"34.0,304.0 34.0,36.7 410.4,304.0\" fill=\"#D9480F\" fill-opacity=\".10\"/><g clip-path=\"url(#b576727274)\" fill=\"none\"><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"36.7\" x2=\"410.4\" y2=\"304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><polyline points=\"34.0,36.7 222.2,304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" stroke-opacity=\".6\"/><polyline points=\"36.6,-9414.8 39.2,-4555.5 41.8,-2935.6 44.4,-2125.7 46.9,-1639.8 49.5,-1315.8 52.1,-1084.4 54.7,-910.9 57.3,-775.9 59.9,-667.9 62.5,-579.5 65.1,-505.9 67.6,-443.6 70.2,-390.2 72.8,-343.9 75.4,-303.4 78.0,-267.7 80.6,-235.9 83.2,-207.5 85.8,-181.9 88.3,-158.8 90.9,-137.8 93.5,-118.6 96.1,-101.0 98.7,-84.8 101.3,-69.8 103.9,-56.0 106.5,-43.1 109.0,-31.1 111.6,-20.0 114.2,-9.5 116.8,0.3 119.4,9.5 122.0,18.1 124.6,26.3 127.2,34.0 129.7,41.3 132.3,48.2 134.9,54.8 137.5,61.0 140.1,67.0 142.7,72.6 145.3,78.0 147.9,83.1 150.4,88.0 153.0,92.7 155.6,97.2 158.2,101.5 160.8,105.7 163.4,109.6 166.0,113.4 168.6,117.1 171.1,120.6 173.7,124.0 176.3,127.3 178.9,130.4 181.5,133.5 184.1,136.4 186.7,139.3 189.3,142.0 191.8,144.7 194.4,147.2 197.0,149.7 199.6,152.1 202.2,154.5 204.8,156.7 207.4,158.9 210.0,161.1 212.5,163.1 215.1,165.2 217.7,167.1 220.3,169.0 222.9,170.9 225.5,172.7 228.1,174.4 230.7,176.1 233.2,177.8 235.8,179.4 238.4,181.0 241.0,182.5 243.6,184.0 246.2,185.5 248.8,186.9 251.4,188.3 253.9,189.7 256.5,191.0 259.1,192.3 261.7,193.6 264.3,194.8 266.9,196.0 269.5,197.2 272.1,198.4 274.6,199.5 277.2,200.6 279.8,201.7 282.4,202.8 285.0,203.8 287.6,204.8 290.2,205.8 292.8,206.8 295.3,207.8 297.9,208.7 300.5,209.6 303.1,210.5 305.7,211.4 308.3,212.3 310.9,213.2 313.5,214.0 316.0,214.8 318.6,215.6 321.2,216.4 323.8,217.2 326.4,218.0 329.0,218.7 331.6,219.5 334.2,220.2 336.7,220.9 339.3,221.6 341.9,222.3 344.5,223.0 347.1,223.7 349.7,224.3 352.3,225.0 354.9,225.6 357.4,226.2 360.0,226.9 362.6,227.5 365.2,228.1 367.8,228.7 370.4,229.2 373.0,229.8 375.6,230.4 378.1,230.9 380.7,231.5 383.3,232.0 385.9,232.5 388.5,233.1 391.1,233.6 393.7,234.1 396.3,234.6 398.8,235.1 401.4,235.6 404.0,236.0 406.6,236.5 409.2,237.0 411.8,237.4 414.4,237.9 417.0,238.3 419.5,238.8 422.1,239.2 424.7,239.6 427.3,240.1 429.9,240.5 432.5,240.9 435.1,241.3 437.7,241.7 440.2,242.1 442.8,242.5 445.4,242.9 448.0,243.3\" stroke=\"#0062C4\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/></g><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"304.0\" x2=\"448.0\" y2=\"304.0\" stroke=\"#111\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"304.0\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"10.0\" stroke=\"#111\"/><polyline points=\"34.0,36.7 410.4,304.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"2.6\"/><line x1=\"410.4\" y1=\"304.0\" x2=\"410.4\" y2=\"308.0\" stroke=\"#111\"/><text x=\"410.4\" y=\"319.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text><line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"36.7\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"36.7\" stroke=\"#111\"/><text x=\"28.0\" y=\"40.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><circle cx=\"34.0\" cy=\"36.7\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"410.4\" cy=\"304.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\"/><polygon points=\"133.8,107.6 122.2,104.5 127.1,97.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><polygon points=\"310.6,233.1 322.2,236.2 317.3,243.1\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"222.2\" cy=\"170.4\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#111\"/><text x=\"227.2\" y=\"165.4\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">(4, 2)</text><text x=\"38.1\" y=\"118.5\" font-size=\"10\">at (0, 4): 4 vs 0</text><text x=\"226.3\" y=\"252.2\" font-size=\"10\">at (8, 0): 0 vs 4</text></svg>", "picture_note": "Arrows: which way bang for the buck pushes. A label such as \"at (0, 12): 6 vs 0\" means that at that point the bang is 6 on x against 0 on y. With several pieces it starts with the piece number."}, {"n": 4, "caption": "After the first 2 of x, its price goes from 1 to 3.", "solution": "<h4>The change</h4><p>After the first 2 of x, its price goes from 1 to 3.</p><h4>Before</h4><p>The best was <math><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, with <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math> at <math><mn>8</mn></math>.</p><h4>The new budget</h4><p><div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></math></div><div><math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></div></p><h4>What the utility says</h4><p><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, <math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p>Bang for the buck: compare <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mfrac></math> with <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mfrac></math>, using each piece's own prices. Higher on <math><mi>x</mi></math>: more <math><mi>x</mi></math>. Equal: stop.</p><h4>Piece 1: <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></h4><p>Equal bang: <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> = <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, so <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math>. Put this into the line: <math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, so <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>That is off this piece, which runs from <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> to <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>Bang for the buck at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mn>4</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so more <math><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p>So on this whole piece move right, to <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><h4>Piece 2: <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></h4><p>Equal bang: <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> = <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, so <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>x</mi></math>. Put this into the line: <math><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math>, so <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>.</p><p>That is on this piece.</p><p>Bang for the buck at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so less <math><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><h4>The kink</h4><p><math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: before it, with prices <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, 3 against 1: more <math><mi>x</mi></math>; after it, with prices <math><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, 1 against 1: equal. So stop at this kink.</p><h4>Where it stops</h4><p>Bang for the buck stops at one point only, <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. So no comparison of utilities is needed.</p><h4>Answer</h4><p><b>The best bundle is <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, with <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>.</b></p><h4>What changed</h4><p><b>The answer changes.</b> Utility falls from <math><mn>8</mn></math> to <math><mn>6</mn></math>.</p>", "picture": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"budget pieces and bang for the buck\" style=\"font-size:12px\"><defs><clipPath id=\"b1643866443\"><rect x=\"34\" y=\"10\" width=\"414\" height=\"294\"/></clipPath></defs><polygon points=\"34.0,304.0 34.0,36.7 128.1,103.5 222.2,304.0\" fill=\"#D9480F\" fill-opacity=\".10\"/><g clip-path=\"url(#b1643866443)\" fill=\"none\"><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"36.7\" x2=\"410.4\" y2=\"304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"-96.9\" x2=\"222.2\" y2=\"304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><polyline points=\"34.0,36.7 410.4,304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" stroke-opacity=\".6\"/><polyline points=\"36.6,-6985.1 39.2,-3340.6 41.8,-2125.7 44.4,-1518.3 46.9,-1153.8 49.5,-910.9 52.1,-737.3 54.7,-607.2 57.3,-505.9 59.9,-424.9 62.5,-358.7 65.1,-303.4 67.6,-256.7 70.2,-216.7 72.8,-181.9 75.4,-151.6 78.0,-124.8 80.6,-101.0 83.2,-79.6 85.8,-60.5 88.3,-43.1 90.9,-27.3 93.5,-12.9 96.1,0.3 98.7,12.4 101.3,23.6 103.9,34.0 106.5,43.7 109.0,52.6 111.6,61.0 114.2,68.9 116.8,76.2 119.4,83.1 122.0,89.6 124.6,95.7 127.2,101.5 129.7,107.0 132.3,112.2 134.9,117.1 137.5,121.8 140.1,126.2 142.7,130.4 145.3,134.5 147.9,138.3 150.4,142