 y2=\"103.5\" stroke=\"#111\"/><text x=\"28.0\" y=\"107.0\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><line x1=\"30.0\" y1=\"36.7\" x2=\"34.0\" y2=\"36.7\" stroke=\"#111\"/><text x=\"28.0\" y=\"40.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><circle cx=\"34.0\" cy=\"36.7\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"128.1\" cy=\"103.5\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"222.2\" cy=\"304.0\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"222.2\" cy=\"170.4\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 1.5\"/><polygon points=\"86.7,74.2 75.1,71.1 80.0,64.2\" fill=\"#111\"/><polygon points=\"172.1,197.5 180.7,205.8 173.1,209.4\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"128.1\" cy=\"103.5\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#111\"/><text x=\"133.1\" y=\"98.5\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\">(2, 3)</text><line x1=\"222.2\" y1=\"170.4\" x2=\"231.2\" y2=\"161.4\" stroke=\"#777\" stroke-width=\".6\"/><text x=\"231.2\" y=\"161.4\" font-size=\"10\">off this piece</text><line x1=\"81.0\" y1=\"70.1\" x2=\"109.0\" y2=\"42.1\" stroke=\"#777\" stroke-width=\".6\"/><text x=\"109.0\" y=\"42.1\" font-size=\"10\">1: at (2, 3): 3 vs 1</text><text x=\"70.1\" y=\"218.8\" font-size=\"10\">2: at (4, 0): 0 vs 2</text></svg>", "picture_note": "Arrows: which way bang for the buck pushes. A label such as \"at (0, 12): 6 vs 0\" means that at that point the bang is 6 on x against 0 on y. With several pieces it starts with the piece number."}, {"n": 5, "caption": "Preferences change: <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.", "solution": "<h4>The change</h4><p>Preferences change: <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p><h4>Before</h4><p>The best was <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, with <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math> at <math><mn>6</mn></math>.</p><h4>The budget</h4><p><div><math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></math></div><div><math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math> for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></div></p><h4>What the utility says</h4><p><math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, <math><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>.</p><p>Bang for the buck: compare <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mfrac></math> with <math><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">MU</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mfrac></math>, using each piece's own prices. Higher on <math><mi>x</mi></math>: more <math><mi>x</mi></math>. Equal: stop.</p><h4>Piece 1: <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></h4><p>Equal bang: <math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> = <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, so <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Put this into the line: <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>, so <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>That is off this piece, which runs from <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> to <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.</p><p>Bang for the buck at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mn>16</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so more <math><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p>So on this whole piece move right, to <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><h4>Piece 2: <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></h4><p>Equal bang: <math><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> = <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, so <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. Put this into the line: <math><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math>, so <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p>That is off this piece, which runs from <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> to <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p>Bang for the buck at <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> on <math><mi>x</mi></math> against <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math> on <math><mi>y</mi></math>, so less <math><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p>So on this whole piece move left, to <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><h4>The kink</h4><p><math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>: before it, with prices <math><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, 9 against 6: more <math><mi>x</mi></math>; after it, with prices <math><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, 3 against 6: less <math><mi>x</mi></math>. So stop at this kink.</p><h4>Where it stops</h4><p>Bang for the buck stops at one point only, <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. So no comparison of utilities is needed.</p><h4>Answer</h4><p><b>The best bundle is <math><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, with <math><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>.</b></p><h4>What changed</h4><p><b>The answer stays: the best bundle doesn't move.</b> The utility function is new, so its numbers can't be compared with the old ones.</p>", "picture": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 460 330\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"budget pieces and bang for the buck\" style=\"font-size:12px\"><defs><clipPath id=\"b3438888277\"><rect x=\"34\" y=\"10\" width=\"414\" height=\"294\"/></clipPath></defs><polygon points=\"34.0,304.0 34.0,36.7 222.2,103.5 410.4,304.0\" fill=\"#D9480F\" fill-opacity=\".10\"/><g clip-path=\"url(#b3438888277)\" fill=\"none\"><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"36.7\" x2=\"786.7\" y2=\"304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><line x1=\"34.0\" y1=\"-96.9\" x2=\"410.4\" y2=\"304.0\" stroke=\"#D9480F\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-opacity=\".35\"/><polyline points=\"36.6,-1405.5 39.2,-904.8 41.8,-683.0 44.4,-550.7 46.9,-460.5 49.5,-393.9 52.1,-342.1 54.7,-300.4 57.3,-265.8 59.9,-236.6 62.5,-211.4 65.1,-189.5 67.6,-170.1 70.2,-152.9 72.8,-137.4 75.4,-123.4 78.0,-110.6 80.6,-98.9 83.2,-88.2 85.8,-78.3 88.3,-69.0 90.9,-60.5 93.5,-52.5 96.1,-44.9 98.7,-37.9 101.3,-31.3 103.9,-25.0 106.5,-19.1 109.0,-13.4 111.6,-8.1 114.2,-3.0 116.8,1.8 119.4,6.4 122.0,10.8 124.6,15.0 127.2,19.1 129.7,23.0 132.3,26.7 134.9,30.3 137.5,33.7 140.1,37.0 142.7,40.2 145.3,43.3 147.9,46.3 150.4,49.2 153.0,52.0 155.6,54.6 158.2,57.3 160.8,59.8 163.4,62.2 166.0,64.6 168.6,66.9 171.1,69.2 173.7,71.4 176.3,73.5 178.9,75.6 181.5,77.6 184.1,79.5 186.7,81.4 189.3,83.3 191.8,85.1 194.4,86.9 197.0,88.6 199.6,90.3 202.2,92.0 204.8,93.6 207.4,95.2 210.0,96.7 212.5,98.2 215.1,99.7 217.7,101.1 220.3,102.5 222.9,103.9 225.5,105.3 228.1,106.6 230.7,107.9 233.2,109.2 235.8,110.4 238.4,111.7 241.0,112.9 243.6,114.1 246.2,115.2 248.8,116.4 251.4,117.5 253.9,118.6 256.5,119.7 259.1,120.7 261.7,121.8 264.3,122.8 266.9,123.8 269.5,124.8 272.1,125.8 274.6,126.7 277.2,127.7 279.8,128.6 282.4,129.5 285.0,130.4 287.6,131.3 290.2,132.2 292.8,133.1 295.3,133.9 297.9,134.7 300.5,135.6 303.1,136.4 305.7,137.2 308.3,138.0 310.9,138.7 313.5,13